  "hypothesis_id": "H-PO03-WA-020",
  "hypothesis_outcome": "REFUTED",
  "hypothesis_outcome_reading": "Half of the hypothesis holds and half of it does not, and the design says which half. Anonymization does reduce producer-identity bias, completely and measurably: worst-case identity swing falls from 49 weighted points to 0 with the same reviewer and the same bias function. The ordering gate contributes nothing to that reduction. The second conjunct fails: the mechanism does not catch the seeded false claim, because the claim is caught by running a repository control and refuted by its exit status, and the mechanism contains nothing that runs anything. Held fully on with a credulous adjudicator, the mechanism catches the claim in 0/4 to 0/4 permutations. Anonymization earns a narrower credit than the hypothesis claims: it stops a biased reviewer discounting a refutation the probe already produced, worth one permutation of four in the one cell where standing is visible and the control is run.",
